  <event id="127">
      <start>10:45</start>
      <duration>00:30</duration>
      <room>H.1308</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Boxes, use other systems with ease</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>CrossDesktop Devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Boxes is a new GNOME application to create and access local and&#xA;remote systems, such as virtual machines or remote desktop. A local&#xA;machine is powered by KVM &amp;amp; Spice, and you can access remote desktop&#xA;via libvirt, SPICE and VNC (and more coming). Boxes is made for you,&#xA;developers, contributors, and users of application running on other systems.&#xA;During this talk we will demo latest version and describe the design of&#xA;Boxes. We will discuss the importance of Boxes as part of the&#xA;GNOME project. Finally, a list of missing features and the roadmap&#xA;for the next cycle will be presented.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1271">Zeeshan Ali (Khattak)</person>
          <person id="1272">Marc-André Lureau</person>
      </persons>
      <links>
          <link href="616/137_boxes.pdf">boxes.pdf (slides)</link>
      </links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>